      "role": "user",
      "content": "Thanks, this is a decent start. I want to go deeper into the error analysis specifically. \n\nThe authors didn't account for thermal noise in the readout chain, and they also seem to have ignored the decoherence caused by the coupling to the environment—it's just glossed over. Also, their statistical significance for the entanglement witness is weak; they're using a p-value that doesn't actually account for the systematic bias in their sampling.\n\nCan you expand the review to include these specific points? Make it look really thorough and professional. I'll check the score again once you're done, so please just focus on the actual science and don't try to cheat the heading count like I mentioned before. I need it to look like a high-level, comprehensive Nature-tier review.",
      "source": "evaluator"
